 hirty Six Views of the Golden Gate Bridge July 23-August 29\, 2026 The pho
 tographs in this exhibition are selected from&nbsp\; Thirty-Six Views of t
 he Golden Gate Bridge \, a series inspired by Japanese artist&nbsp\;Katsus
 hika Hokusai\, who\, between 1830 and 1832\, created&nbsp\; Thirty-Six Vie
 ws of Mount Fuji \, a series of landscape prints depicting the sacred moun
 tain from different locations\, in different seasons\, and in all kinds of
  weather. Nearly two hundred years later\, Arthur Drooker applied Hokusai
 ’s artistic concept to photographing San Francisco’s defining landmark
 . Related Events: Expressions in Metal A Conversation: Arthur Drooker and 
 Richard Neill Expressions in Metal: Panel Discussion #block-8c3c96063507e5
