  Dates: September 17 - October 24\, 2026 Opening Reception: Thursday\, Sep
 tember 17\, 5:30-7:30pm RSVP HERE It’s Not Trash: Reclaiming and Transfo
 rming&nbsp\; combines a selection of 37 artists from Recology San Francisc
 o’s Artist in Residence (AIR) Program and six invited artists from the B
 ay Area.&nbsp\; All participating artists created their work from reclaime
 d materials\, shifting what is perceived of as&nbsp\;“trash” to reimag
 ined art objects.&nbsp\; The exhibit continues in our North Gallery with&n
 bsp\; Strictly Local: Piecing It Together in Sonoma County&nbsp\; where st
 udents\, community members\, and individual artists encourage us to questi
 on our relationship with what we consider “waste”.&nbsp\; &nbsp\; Cura
 tor: Lisa Lightman&nbsp\;&nbsp\; A Partnership in Action: &nbsp\;This exhi
 bition is a community partnership with&nbsp\;Recology Artist-in-Residence 
 Program\,&nbsp\;San Francisco\; Petaluma's Reuse Alliance\; and the Recolo
